v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy","html_url":"https://github.com/myblindy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-07T14:08:04Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T14:13:24Z","body":"> I agree this PR is a good solution. I will close #106066. Although #106066 is compatible with this PR, it would suppress the warnings. Caching StringName is still the best.\r\n\r\nI mean, it doesn’t have to disable the warnings. Slap a framework attribute on the new string parameters (like `[StringNameParameter]` or something) and I can add it to the list of things it checks and auto-fixes. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2858743510/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2858847353","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106096#issuecomment-2858847353","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106096","id":2858847353,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6qZox5","user":{"login":"beicause","id":75941842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1OTQxODQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75941842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause","html_url":"https://github.com/beicause","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-07T14:36:53Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T14:36:53Z","body":"I'm not familiar with Roslyn Analyzer, but #106066 still isn't worth adding the complexity. In places where performance matters, there's no reason to use strings instead of constructing StringName in advance.\r\n \r\nBy the way, the warnings and auto fixes should also be provided for `NodePath`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2858847353/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2858944682","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106096#issuecomment-2858944682","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106096","id":2858944682,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6qaAiq","user":{"login":"myblindy","id":541998,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MTk5OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/541998?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy","html_url":"https://github.com/myblindy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-07T15:01:43Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T15:01:43Z","body":"> I'm not familiar with Roslyn Analyzer, but #106066 still isn't worth adding the complexity. In places where performance matters, there's no reason to use strings instead of constructing StringName in advance.\r\n\r\nI strongly disagree with that. In fact I believe that the `StringName` abstraction should be hidden from the user completely, like it is in GDScript (and it would be with the implicit construction operator). We only care about it here because it's written in a way that is very inefficient, and that is an implementation detail. \r\n\r\nGodot C#'s closest competitor is Unity, and they don't require you to create cache variables just to check key/gamepad inputs, for example. Simplicity is king, as long as it doesn't tank framerates. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2858944682/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2858993622","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106096#issuecomment-2858993622","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106096","id":2858993622,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6qaMfW","user":{"login":"myblindy","id":541998,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MTk5OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/541998?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy","html_url":"https://github.com/myblindy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-07T15:12:24Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T15:12:24Z","body":"@raulsntos I updated it as discussed, now it will trigger warnings on every implicit `StringName` construction, and it will auto-correct as many as possible by caching the variable as long as the string used to construct it can be evaluated at compile time. Dynamic implicit `StringName` instances remain highlighted as warnings, but have no code fix available. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2858993622/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2960893853","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106096#issuecomment-2960893853","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106096","id":2960893853,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6we6ed","user":{"login":"Joy-less","id":65855333,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1ODU1MzMz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65855333?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less","html_url":"https://github.com/Joy-less","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-11T00:37:48Z","updated_at":"2025-06-11T00:37:48Z","body":"My opinion is that, while this solution would be better than nothing, I do not like it. There are many cases where you can't use an auto-generated `StringName`, and adding private variable declarations reduces readability to an unacceptable degree.\r\nI much prefer #100452 (or even #106153).\r\n\r\n@raulsntos can I ask for your review of the pull requests involved (especially #100452)?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2960893853/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2968751967","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106096#issuecomment-2968751967","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106096","id":2968751967,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6w849f","user":{"login":"myblindy","id":541998,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MTk5OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/541998?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy","html_url":"https://github.com/myblindy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-13T02:01:30Z","updated_at":"2025-06-13T02:03:01Z","body":"I agree with @Joy-less, C# is a very elegant, very performant language. Having to create static constants by hand because the framework can't handle calling functions with strings is the polar opposite of that.\r\n\r\nHowever, the actual fixes to the problem (holding a cache of `StringName` instances like I proposed in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106153) seems to not be understood by the Godot community. I'm getting all sorts of weird round-about comments about too much memory used (measured in kilobytes), something about strings being GC'd (this has nothing to do with strings, but with `StringName`s), using weak references (when the whole idea is to avoid reallocations by rooting instances), doesn't understand how references aren't rooted across repeated function calls (`_Process`, etc), and on and on. \r\n\r\nIt would help if someone who actually understands the .Net runtime would review these solutions. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2968751967/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]